parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfxivQEpyE1fcXQFgzZBD", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I worked these out by hand without running any simulation, so the profit forecasts (claim) are rough estimates. My working assumptions:\n\n- **Margin per unit:** 6 per unit sold, with shortage penalties of 6 and 5 per unit. That means a missed sale costs about as much as it would have earned.\n- **Order fee:** the 42 per ordering day adds up. Ordering every day costs about 1,180, while ordering every other day costs about 590.\n- **Order timing:** each order is sized to the forecast for the day it arrives (day t + L), with a safety margin. A pooled order covers 2 or 3 days of demand.\n- **Last useful orders:** the last order that still arrives in time is day 26 for item 0 and day 27 for item 1.\n- **Demand spikes:** the forecast has a spike of 69 for item 0 on day 22 and 63 for item 1 on day 23. The orders for these are placed on days 19 and 21 when ordering daily, and pooled into the day-18 and day-20 orders in the every-other-day plans.\n- **Capacity:** in the every-3-days and every-other-day plans, the large orders around day 21–22 come close to the 188-unit warehouse limit. I lowered those orders by hand to stay under it.\n\nI expect the every-other-day plan with a 1.1× margin to do best."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2373, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2378, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 2373}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-12T17:18:48.549Z", "request_id": "req_011CfxivQ3ApRtmCgsgtuMBd"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"